 "read": "Each fixture read twice. (1) STEPControl_Reader as any application reads a STEP file: ReadFile, the model's global and per-entity check (readerFails, readerWarnings), TransferRoots with OpenCascade's standard shape healing, then per solid BRepCheck_Analyzer, every shell closed, no free edges, a point far outside classified OUT, GProp volume and a tight Bnd_Box (AddOptimal, no triangulation, no tolerance) -> valid, volume, box. (2) strict: each MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP / BREP_WITH_VOIDS translated straight from its entities by StepToTopoDS_Builder with none of that healing, then only what a file without pcurves leaves a reader to do (ShapeFix_Wire FixEdgeCurves, FixShifted, FixDegenerated; BRepLib SameParameter \u2014 nothing that moves a vertex, reverses an edge or face, or reorders a loop), then the same checks plus every vertex and edge tolerance still the file's 1e-7 -> strict, strictVolume. The healed read alone passes broken files: with one face's same_sense flipped, the whole solid inside out, one oriented edge reversed or a vertex moved 0.01 mm it still reports a valid solid of the right volume. The strict read rejects all four (and an open shell), which is why it is here.",
